---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro"
---
<Page title="How it works">
	<section class="intro">
		<p class="eyebrow">One value, two beginnings</p>
		<h1>One database. Two ways to read it.</h1>
		<p>
			Astro waits for the atom defaults, renders the stock cards with SPA, and
			attaches the results to each island’s HTML as seed data. The browser
			consumes those values before hydrating the existing cards.
		</p>
		<p>
			A reset calls the default again. Its server value has already been
			consumed, so the client closure calls tRPC for a fresh database read.
			Editing, saving, or reloading a product updates both views. Saving persists
			the count and checks its revision so it cannot silently overwrite another
			stock count.
		</p>
		<p>
			Navigation releases the islands while keeping your shared state alive.
			Returning renders fresh views of your edits. Reload explicitly to fetch new
			data. SSR and tRPC call the same function, backed by a typed SQL query.
		</p>
		<a class="back" href="/">Back to inventory →</a>
	</section>
</Page>
